---
import VersionSwitcher from '../../components/VersionSwitcher.astro';
import LiveBakeRail from '../../components/LiveBakeRail.astro';
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<title>Living Canvas Pivot — aito</title>
	<style>
		body { background:#0a0a0b; color:#e7e7ea; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; padding: 2rem; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.65; }
		h1 { color: #ff5b2e; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
		.subtitle { color: #8a8a93; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 0; }
		h2 { color: #ff5b2e; margin-top: 2rem; }
		pre { background:#111; padding:1rem; overflow:auto; }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<VersionSwitcher />
	<h1>Live Canvas</h1>
	<p class="subtitle">The local CLI companion for aito</p>
	<p><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}hub/`}>← Back to Hub</a></p>

	<h2>Built for tethered workflows and high-end color.</h2>
	<p>Real-time camera tethering, powerful LUT pipelines, and the local tools you reach for when the work actually matters.</p>

	<!-- In a real setup you would render the markdown nicely.
	     For now we link to the raw file in the repo. -->
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/fornevercollective/aito/blob/main/versions/living-canvas/docs/LIVING-CANVAS-ARCHITECTURE-PROPOSAL.md">
			Read the full proposal on GitHub →
		</a>
	</p>

	<h2>Design Tokens</h2>
	<p>The living tokens (aito + Tron + Resolve + filmic) live here:</p>
	<p><code>iterations/living-canvas/src/styles/living-tokens.css</code></p>

	<div style="margin-top: 2rem; padding: 2rem; background: #111113; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #222;">
		<h3 style="margin-top:0;">Install Live Canvas</h3>
		
		<div style="margin: 1.25rem 0;">
			<strong>npm</strong>
			<pre><code>npm install -g @fornevercollective/live-canvas</code></pre>
		</div>

		<div style="margin: 1.25rem 0;">
			<strong>Homebrew</strong>
			<pre><code>brew install fornevercollective/tap/live-canvas</code></pre>
		</div>

		<div>
			<a href="https://github.com/fornevercollective/aito/releases/latest" class="btn" style="display:inline-block; background:#ff5b2e; color:#000; padding:10px 20px; border-radius:6px; text-decoration:none; font-weight:600;">
				Download latest release
			</a>
		</div>
	</div>

	<p style="margin-top:2rem; color:#8a8a93; font-size: 0.9rem;">
		This page contains the technical research and vision. The CLI itself is the practical tool.<br>
		Launch screenshots live in the main site.
	</p>

	<p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #555;">
		Requires Node 22+ • Works with any camera that has a local companion (see the overview live lab tools for examples).
	</p>

	<h2>Live Bake Path (vwall + Tree Walker)</h2>
	<p>One of the key technical explorations in this track is an incremental bake system using a tree-sitter-style edit graph + vwall MediaLadder patterns for efficient variant storage and LOD previews.</p>
	
	<LiveBakeRail />

	<div style="margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid #222;">
		<a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}`} style="color: #ff5b2e; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500;">
			→ Open the Editor →
		</a>
	</div>
</body>
</html>